1
00:00:06,027 --> 00:00:09,447
Why did Mr. Uramawashi
become a lawyer in the first place?

2
00:00:09,531 --> 00:00:11,157
Isn't he a first-class architect?

3
00:00:11,241 --> 00:00:13,243
I'm also a first-class architect.

4
00:00:13,326 --> 00:00:15,703
-I'm talking about Mr. Uramawashi.
-Okay.

5
00:00:15,787 --> 00:00:18,623
Why did you become a lawyer, Ms. Aso?

6
00:00:18,706 --> 00:00:22,335
I admired someone

7
00:00:22,418 --> 00:00:26,548
and wanted to become a lawyer
to justly help people in trouble.

8
00:00:26,631 --> 00:00:27,924
So passionate!

9
00:00:28,007 --> 00:00:29,050
That's lovely.

10
00:00:29,134 --> 00:00:33,138
No, we were talking about
why Mr. Uramawashi became a lawyer.

11
00:00:33,221 --> 00:00:35,807
-No clue, you?
-No.

12
00:00:37,308 --> 00:00:38,935
Why are you so curious?

13
00:00:42,105 --> 00:00:46,192
Some people can't be saved
through legal means alone.

14
00:00:48,403 --> 00:00:49,863
Forget it.

15
00:00:49,946 --> 00:00:51,447
I'm leaving.

16
00:00:51,531 --> 00:00:52,532
Huh? You're--

17
00:00:52,615 --> 00:00:54,450
-Excuse me.
-No, wait.

18
00:00:54,534 --> 00:00:55,827
Thank you for the meal.

19
00:00:55,910 --> 00:00:57,120
You just arrived, though.

20
00:00:57,203 --> 00:00:58,037
Hey!

21
00:01:06,296 --> 00:01:08,423
Here, please use this.

22
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:11,718
No, I couldn't possibly!

23
00:01:11,801 --> 00:01:14,554
Please use it. I live nearby.

24
00:01:19,184 --> 00:01:20,185
Goodbye.

25
00:01:21,019 --> 00:01:22,353
Wait a moment, please.

26
00:01:22,437 --> 00:01:24,022
I'll definitely return it.

27
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:27,442
For now, this is my contact information.

28
00:01:29,652 --> 00:01:30,945
You're a lawyer?

29
00:01:38,703 --> 00:01:40,747
Habu, look.

30
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:54,594
Thank you very much for this.

31
00:01:54,677 --> 00:01:55,803
It's nothing.

32
00:01:58,556 --> 00:02:01,017
My friend's father

33
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:04,270
owns an apartment building
in Konan City, Chiba.

34
00:02:04,354 --> 00:02:05,271
I see.

35
00:02:05,355 --> 00:02:09,525
He's trying to rebuild
that apartment building,

36
00:02:10,276 --> 00:02:12,820
but there's one person who won't vacate.

37
00:02:12,904 --> 00:02:14,739
-Won't vacate?
-Yes.

38
00:02:14,822 --> 00:02:20,620
Under Japanese law, is there any way
we can make that person move out?

39
00:02:21,621 --> 00:02:24,249
At this point, I can't say for sure.

40
00:02:24,332 --> 00:02:26,584
Did your friend consult a lawyer?

41
00:02:27,293 --> 00:02:29,963
Right now, my friend is in Korea.

42
00:02:30,046 --> 00:02:32,382
So he's really in a bind.

43
00:02:34,509 --> 00:02:37,178
Could you tell me the details again?

44
00:02:39,722 --> 00:02:42,642
Isn't it weird to ask a lawyer
to help a friend's father?

45
00:02:42,725 --> 00:02:45,478
You're weirder for stalking
and taking photos of them.

46
00:02:45,561 --> 00:02:48,356
That's not what's important right now.

47
00:02:48,439 --> 00:02:49,732
I'm sorry.

48
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:52,485
Love?

49
00:02:52,568 --> 00:02:53,945
You think so too, right?

50
00:02:54,028 --> 00:02:55,947
No way.

51
00:02:56,030 --> 00:02:58,491
Ms. Aso, with a guy like that?

52
00:02:58,574 --> 00:03:01,369
I didn't think there'd be
eviction issues there.

53
00:03:01,452 --> 00:03:02,912
It's Konan City, right?

54
00:03:02,996 --> 00:03:05,248
Yes, Konan City in Chiba.

55
00:03:05,331 --> 00:03:07,000
Have you been there?

56
00:03:07,083 --> 00:03:09,335
Yes, to film a reenactment show.

57
00:03:09,419 --> 00:03:10,420
To film?

58
00:03:10,503 --> 00:03:13,297
Ms. Asuka used to be an actress.

59
00:03:13,381 --> 00:03:16,926
-What?
-That's how the theater troupe knew you!

60
00:03:20,596 --> 00:03:21,806
This story

61
00:03:23,099 --> 00:03:25,309
might have a blueprint hidden behind it.

62
00:03:35,403 --> 00:03:37,864
VACANT LAND

63
00:03:37,947 --> 00:03:42,577
KONAN CITY 60TH ANNIVERSARY

64
00:03:49,751 --> 00:03:51,169
This way.

65
00:03:55,798 --> 00:03:58,843
Do you happen to know
what your friend's father is like?

66
00:03:58,926 --> 00:04:00,928
No, I don't know him well.

67
00:04:01,429 --> 00:04:03,639
But according to my friend,

68
00:04:03,723 --> 00:04:07,810
he collapsed from overwork last month
and was taken to the hospital.

69
00:04:07,894 --> 00:04:09,604
I see.

70
00:04:09,687 --> 00:04:14,484
Yes, because of that, my friend Taichi
is rushing to settle this.

71
00:04:17,236 --> 00:04:18,738
Excuse me.

72
00:04:19,364 --> 00:04:20,573
Hello?

73
00:04:21,199 --> 00:04:22,408
Mr. Hoshino?

74
00:04:23,326 --> 00:04:25,244
Yes, we'll be there shortly.

75
00:04:25,328 --> 00:04:27,955
HOSHINO APARTMENT

76
00:04:29,624 --> 00:04:31,918
I heard from Taichi.

77
00:04:33,127 --> 00:04:35,254
You are Hyonduk, right?

78
00:04:35,338 --> 00:04:37,757
My name is Donghyuk. Nice to meet you.

79
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:40,510
I'm Aso, a lawyer. Nice to meet you.

80
00:04:47,058 --> 00:04:48,726
It's a parasol.

81
00:04:48,810 --> 00:04:50,144
Thank you.

82
00:04:52,563 --> 00:04:54,482
How many umbrellas does that guy have?

83
00:04:54,565 --> 00:04:55,733
Right?

84
00:04:57,485 --> 00:04:58,528
MUKAI REAL ESTATE

85
00:04:58,611 --> 00:04:59,737
Have a drink.

86
00:05:02,407 --> 00:05:06,285
Mr. Mukai, the snack bar on the first
floor is refusing to vacate, right?

87
00:05:06,369 --> 00:05:08,079
Yes, that's right.

88
00:05:08,162 --> 00:05:11,290
Every day, the noise
from their karaoke is unbearable.

89
00:05:11,374 --> 00:05:13,543
A noise issue? Since when?

90
00:05:15,086 --> 00:05:16,671
For the past three months.

91
00:05:17,588 --> 00:05:20,049
-When was the notice to vacate?
-Six months ago.

92
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:23,511
So they started making noise
after the eviction notice.

93
00:05:23,594 --> 00:05:24,470
Yeah.

94
00:05:32,937 --> 00:05:35,106
Shut up!

95
00:05:35,189 --> 00:05:37,650
What time do you think it is, you idiots?!

96
00:05:37,733 --> 00:05:39,694
Shut up, old man!

97
00:05:39,777 --> 00:05:42,113
It's so noisy I can't sleep, damn it!

98
00:05:42,196 --> 00:05:44,448
That's enough, go home!

99
00:05:44,532 --> 00:05:47,910
Why won't you get out of here, you idiots?

100
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:52,331
You're disrupting my business.
I'll call the police!

101
00:05:52,415 --> 00:05:54,750
And it has been going on for three months?

102
00:05:55,501 --> 00:05:57,170
That's not all.

103
00:05:57,253 --> 00:06:00,923
They leave trash lying around,
and crows and stray cats mess with it,

104
00:06:01,007 --> 00:06:02,925
making clean-up a nightmare.

105
00:06:03,009 --> 00:06:05,803
I've been warning them too.

106
00:06:05,887 --> 00:06:08,973
Isn't that kind of behavior
just harassment?

107
00:06:10,516 --> 00:06:11,726
Mr. Hoshino.

108
00:06:12,310 --> 00:06:16,689
As I've mentioned before,
what if we just sell the--

109
00:06:16,772 --> 00:06:19,150
Why am I the one
getting thrown of out here, moron?!

110
00:06:19,233 --> 00:06:22,236
Please calm down. I'm just--

111
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:25,072
I will absolutely not sell!

112
00:06:25,156 --> 00:06:27,408
I will never…

113
00:06:28,159 --> 00:06:29,619
-I won't leave!
-You okay?

114
00:06:31,913 --> 00:06:34,707
I already said I wasn't leaving!

115
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:35,917
Can you think it over?

116
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,838
Listen up,
I've been here for over five years.

117
00:06:42,381 --> 00:06:46,177
Fishermen, construction workers, farmers.

118
00:06:46,719 --> 00:06:50,348
All kinds of people drop by
and enjoy themselves here.

119
00:06:51,057 --> 00:06:55,394
Well, I suppose to a fancy lawyer
like you, they're just nobody.

120
00:06:55,478 --> 00:06:57,146
No, that's not true.

121
00:06:57,772 --> 00:07:01,442
That old man,
suddenly telling us to leave. Ridiculous!

122
00:07:02,151 --> 00:07:06,197
But Mr. Hoshino has been asking you
to vacate for six months.

123
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:09,325
Well, depending on how things go…

124
00:07:11,244 --> 00:07:13,412
Maybe I would consider it.

125
00:07:14,413 --> 00:07:15,498
Ten million yen?!

126
00:07:15,581 --> 00:07:18,459
That is just what they are demanding.

127
00:07:19,001 --> 00:07:21,712
It's obvious they're just after the money.

128
00:07:21,796 --> 00:07:23,548
Kick them out already.

129
00:07:23,631 --> 00:07:27,009
If you're a lawyer, you can do that,
right? Threaten them with the law.

130
00:07:27,677 --> 00:07:32,390
Under the Land and Building Leases Act,
tenants are protected by law too.

131
00:07:32,473 --> 00:07:34,850
-So, if they say no, we can't force them?
-Yes.

132
00:07:34,934 --> 00:07:37,687
That's how strong
the tenant's position is.

133
00:07:39,021 --> 00:07:42,316
However, if there is a legitimate reason,
you can evict them.

134
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,402
A legitimate reason?

135
00:07:44,485 --> 00:07:47,863
For example, deterioration of the building
or breach of contract.

136
00:07:47,947 --> 00:07:51,075
However, since there is no clear
legal definition,

137
00:07:51,158 --> 00:07:53,244
the other party might refuse it.

138
00:07:53,869 --> 00:07:55,162
What happens then?

139
00:07:55,246 --> 00:07:56,372
A lawsuit.

140
00:07:56,455 --> 00:07:57,415
What?

141
00:07:57,915 --> 00:08:00,293
Back in the day, a building owner I knew

142
00:08:00,376 --> 00:08:02,920
had a dispute with tenants
that lasted for a year.

143
00:08:03,004 --> 00:08:04,755
-Wow.
-Seriously?

144
00:08:04,839 --> 00:08:05,798
That long?

145
00:08:05,881 --> 00:08:11,846
Also, I checked and they haven't violated
the contract and have paid rent on time.

146
00:08:11,929 --> 00:08:15,016
So, what we can use as leverage
in negotiations

147
00:08:15,099 --> 00:08:17,518
is the noise disturbance you mentioned.

148
00:08:18,561 --> 00:08:21,147
Making excessive noise
can be grounds for eviction.

149
00:08:21,230 --> 00:08:25,151
So, as long as we have evidence,
we can advance negotiations in our favor.

150
00:08:26,902 --> 00:08:28,946
I'm counting on you for that.

151
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:30,698
Yes, I understand.

152
00:08:32,408 --> 00:08:33,701
Here you go.

153
00:08:33,784 --> 00:08:35,328
Huh? Did you order this?

154
00:08:35,411 --> 00:08:36,662
No, I didn't order it.

155
00:08:36,746 --> 00:08:38,122
It's on the house.

156
00:08:38,205 --> 00:08:41,459
-Oh, my.
-Thank you.

157
00:08:46,297 --> 00:08:49,967
This case is not related
to Uramawashi, is it?

158
00:08:50,051 --> 00:08:51,469
It isn't.

159
00:08:52,345 --> 00:08:55,348
You cannot allow him to get involved.

160
00:08:55,431 --> 00:08:57,808
I won't let him lay a single finger on it.

161
00:08:57,892 --> 00:08:59,602
This is my case.

162
00:09:11,489 --> 00:09:15,451
YUKARI ASO

163
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:20,164
Mr. Uramawashi, can you hear me?

164
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:22,249
What is it?

165
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:26,337
Since I'm taking on a case,
I'll probably visit you less often.

166
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:29,006
Should I help you with your case?

167
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:31,801
No, thank you. I can do it by myself.

168
00:09:31,884 --> 00:09:35,638
Definitely don't do
anything strange, okay?

169
00:09:48,651 --> 00:09:50,069
SNACK BAR KIYOMI

170
00:09:53,364 --> 00:09:56,200
I wish Hot Spring Inn Wakaba
was available.

171
00:09:56,283 --> 00:09:59,286
Look at this.
An open-air bath with a sauna.

172
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:01,080
It would've been so great.

173
00:10:01,163 --> 00:10:04,041
It was rejected instantly.
It would have been--

174
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:06,919
Why?

175
00:10:07,837 --> 00:10:08,838
A mosquito.

176
00:10:09,422 --> 00:10:11,048
Tell me before you slap me.

177
00:10:11,132 --> 00:10:12,049
Sorry.

178
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:13,843
What a shock.

179
00:10:17,555 --> 00:10:19,890
SNACK BAR KIYOMI

180
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:24,228
-Huh?
-What?

181
00:10:24,311 --> 00:10:26,021
It seems this lot is vacant.

182
00:10:26,105 --> 00:10:28,315
Is that so? Let's split up and search.

183
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:29,400
Yes.

184
00:10:30,317 --> 00:10:32,737
Oh my.

185
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:34,530
Noise?

186
00:10:35,281 --> 00:10:37,116
Let me see…

187
00:10:38,743 --> 00:10:42,496
It's a bit far, so I'm not sure.

188
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:44,874
Is that so?

189
00:10:44,957 --> 00:10:46,751
-I'm sorry.
-It's fine.

190
00:11:04,685 --> 00:11:06,771
Wait, are you going to stay here?

191
00:11:06,854 --> 00:11:08,606
I got the okay from Mr. Mukai.

192
00:11:08,689 --> 00:11:11,275
Thank you for agreeing as well,
Mr. Hoshino.

193
00:11:11,776 --> 00:11:13,402
Now that it's come to this,

194
00:11:13,486 --> 00:11:16,864
I will get evidence of this noisy behavior
no matter what.

195
00:11:22,912 --> 00:11:25,372
But there's no electricity or gas here.

196
00:11:25,456 --> 00:11:27,666
As long as there's water, it's okay.

197
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:32,296
SNACK BAR KIYOMI

198
00:11:43,182 --> 00:11:44,767
That old man…

199
00:11:45,601 --> 00:11:47,895
I think he's a kind person, deep down.

200
00:11:48,646 --> 00:11:51,649
Like how I am an architect deep down.

201
00:11:56,820 --> 00:12:00,324
Habu, I bought rice balls
from the convenience store.

202
00:12:00,407 --> 00:12:02,368
Do you want tuna mayo or kelp?

203
00:12:02,451 --> 00:12:03,827
I want salmon.

204
00:12:03,911 --> 00:12:05,120
What?

205
00:12:05,204 --> 00:12:06,330
You…

206
00:12:06,413 --> 00:12:09,542
I walked 20 minutes to get here, you know.

207
00:12:09,625 --> 00:12:10,918
Another customer came.

208
00:12:11,001 --> 00:12:12,086
What?

209
00:12:12,169 --> 00:12:14,547
Business sure is booming.

210
00:12:35,734 --> 00:12:38,112
Hey, another beer!

211
00:12:38,195 --> 00:12:39,405
Coming up!

212
00:12:45,286 --> 00:12:47,746
MUKAI REAL ESTATE

213
00:12:49,957 --> 00:12:51,166
What?

214
00:12:53,377 --> 00:12:54,837
Hold on…

215
00:13:31,206 --> 00:13:34,084
KONAN CITY
DO NOT DISPOSE OF ITEMS HERE

216
00:13:38,589 --> 00:13:42,801
It seems the snack bar owner
and Mr. Mukai are talking.

217
00:13:42,885 --> 00:13:44,136
Understood.

218
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:49,433
Mr. Mukai left the owner
and is walking toward the town.

219
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:51,769
Look into his movements for me.

220
00:13:51,852 --> 00:13:52,811
Got it.

221
00:13:58,317 --> 00:13:59,818
KONAN CITY OFFICE

222
00:14:10,037 --> 00:14:13,624
Next, according to Habu,
there seems to be some trouble

223
00:14:13,707 --> 00:14:16,460
between Mukai Real Estate
and this coffee shop.

224
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:19,672
I looked up the court records.

225
00:14:20,589 --> 00:14:24,218
Surprisingly,
Mukai was sued in 2016, 2017,

226
00:14:24,301 --> 00:14:27,721
and in 2020, it seems.

227
00:14:27,805 --> 00:14:29,014
What were the claims?

228
00:14:29,098 --> 00:14:31,392
Damages due to extortion and fraud.

229
00:14:31,976 --> 00:14:35,688
All of them seem to have been settled
with a small settlement fee, though.

230
00:14:36,438 --> 00:14:37,439
Hello.

231
00:14:38,065 --> 00:14:40,693
Ms. Aso! Your shoulder is a bit dirty.

232
00:14:40,776 --> 00:14:43,278
I need to confirm something.
I'll leave right away.

233
00:14:43,821 --> 00:14:47,700
Another 20 million yen.
That's quite a lot.

234
00:14:48,659 --> 00:14:51,286
Is your case going smoothly?

235
00:14:52,746 --> 00:14:55,499
It has nothing to do with you,
Mr. Uramawashi.

236
00:14:56,709 --> 00:15:01,380
It's too hard for you
to handle alone after all.

237
00:15:08,303 --> 00:15:11,849
I do not approve of your methods.

238
00:15:12,641 --> 00:15:16,145
I believe just methods
can still save people.

239
00:15:17,229 --> 00:15:20,441
What counts as being just to you?

240
00:15:33,328 --> 00:15:35,164
Being faithful to the law.

241
00:15:36,123 --> 00:15:38,417
That is what it means to me.

242
00:15:39,293 --> 00:15:40,210
Excuse me.

243
00:15:48,010 --> 00:15:49,011
JUSTICE'S FORM

244
00:15:49,094 --> 00:15:51,722
You can't save people with just that.

245
00:15:55,017 --> 00:15:57,061
To be honest,

246
00:15:57,144 --> 00:16:01,106
I probably couldn't have solved
the previous cases without him.

247
00:16:01,607 --> 00:16:03,817
But I just can't accept it.

248
00:16:03,901 --> 00:16:07,571
So this time, you want to solve it
all by yourself, right?

249
00:16:07,654 --> 00:16:08,614
Yes.

250
00:16:09,490 --> 00:16:13,827
Well, eviction cases are difficult.

251
00:16:13,911 --> 00:16:16,038
Both sides have their own arguments.

252
00:16:16,872 --> 00:16:18,791
That's true.

253
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:23,962
Sometimes I wonder why
he's so attached to that place.

254
00:16:25,297 --> 00:16:26,507
I'm sure

255
00:16:28,008 --> 00:16:30,302
he has his own reasons.

256
00:16:30,886 --> 00:16:32,096
Reasons?

257
00:16:34,014 --> 00:16:35,849
Is it really that run-down?

258
00:16:36,683 --> 00:16:39,228
I think it used to be a thriving town…

259
00:16:39,311 --> 00:16:41,313
It's Konan City in Chiba.

260
00:16:44,233 --> 00:16:45,526
Ms. Shiramoto?

261
00:16:46,985 --> 00:16:48,112
Oh, sorry.

262
00:16:48,695 --> 00:16:49,822
It's nothing.

263
00:16:53,367 --> 00:16:55,744
SNACK BAR KIYOMI

264
00:16:55,828 --> 00:16:57,996
Could you please hear me out?

265
00:16:58,080 --> 00:17:02,000
You're so persistent. It's annoying!

266
00:17:10,092 --> 00:17:12,427
I want a place ten minutes
from the station,

267
00:17:12,511 --> 00:17:14,179
and over 20 square meters.

268
00:17:14,263 --> 00:17:15,514
Understood.

269
00:17:15,597 --> 00:17:18,809
I'll find one right away.
Please wait a moment.

270
00:17:27,276 --> 00:17:28,944
-Excuse me.
-Sure.

271
00:17:32,948 --> 00:17:34,741
Mukai Real Estate.

272
00:17:37,870 --> 00:17:40,330
So you've made up your mind.

273
00:17:40,414 --> 00:17:41,832
That's wise of you.

274
00:17:42,541 --> 00:17:43,625
Yes.

275
00:17:44,418 --> 00:17:45,377
Yes.

276
00:17:46,295 --> 00:17:48,589
Yes.

277
00:17:52,759 --> 00:17:54,011
Yes.

278
00:18:04,354 --> 00:18:05,814
Sorry to keep you waiting.

279
00:18:05,898 --> 00:18:07,900
Thank you very much.

280
00:18:08,567 --> 00:18:10,777
Cheers.

281
00:18:10,861 --> 00:18:12,112
Welcome.

282
00:18:12,196 --> 00:18:13,322
May I sit here?

283
00:18:13,405 --> 00:18:15,032
Of course. Go ahead.

284
00:18:15,115 --> 00:18:16,408
A beer, please.

285
00:18:16,491 --> 00:18:20,495
Coming up. Hold on a moment.

286
00:18:20,579 --> 00:18:22,331
Beer.

287
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:25,542
You're staring too much!

288
00:18:27,085 --> 00:18:29,379
Why is that guy here?

289
00:18:29,463 --> 00:18:30,297
Young man.

290
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:33,091
I don't often see handsome guys
like you around here.

291
00:18:33,175 --> 00:18:36,053
Thank you very much. I came here for work.

292
00:18:36,136 --> 00:18:38,388
This place is so nice and peaceful.

293
00:18:38,472 --> 00:18:39,890
Are you from Korea?

294
00:18:39,973 --> 00:18:40,974
Yes.

295
00:18:41,058 --> 00:18:44,144
That's perfect. We serve
some delicious makgeolli.

296
00:18:44,228 --> 00:18:46,813
-Makgeolli?
-Yes.

297
00:18:50,525 --> 00:18:53,028
-Thank you very much.
-Please come again.

298
00:18:58,242 --> 00:18:59,368
Thanks for the drinks.

299
00:18:59,451 --> 00:19:01,662
What? Hey, wait!

300
00:19:01,745 --> 00:19:03,038
Wait!

301
00:19:24,226 --> 00:19:26,603
It's an emergency.

302
00:19:26,687 --> 00:19:30,023
That guy might be staying overnight.

303
00:19:32,943 --> 00:19:35,237
Hey, it's already ten o'clock.

304
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:36,822
Oh, that's right.

305
00:19:39,324 --> 00:19:40,909
MUSIC

306
00:19:40,993 --> 00:19:42,369
Hey, what's that for?

307
00:19:42,452 --> 00:19:43,745
Don't complain.

308
00:19:43,829 --> 00:19:46,331
So scary. You never bothered before!

309
00:19:46,415 --> 00:19:48,750
I have my problems too, you know.

310
00:19:48,834 --> 00:19:50,168
The heck?

311
00:19:55,215 --> 00:19:57,050
I have cold drinks too.

312
00:19:57,134 --> 00:19:58,885
You're so thoughtful.

313
00:20:00,262 --> 00:20:03,181
How is the noise?

314
00:20:03,265 --> 00:20:07,269
I could hear it until a little while ago,
but it has settled down now.

315
00:20:07,978 --> 00:20:09,855
That's strange.

316
00:20:09,938 --> 00:20:12,524
There were tons of guests
in the shop though.

317
00:20:13,233 --> 00:20:16,236
I just went in there to check it out.

318
00:20:17,321 --> 00:20:18,613
How was it?

319
00:20:19,156 --> 00:20:21,867
I don't think it was such a bad place.

320
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:26,413
The owner was friendly.
She even gave me some makgeolli.

321
00:20:26,496 --> 00:20:28,623
I see.

322
00:20:28,707 --> 00:20:33,503
I guess I will update Taichi in Seoul
about the current situation.

323
00:20:33,587 --> 00:20:35,672
Yes, thank you very much.

324
00:20:37,174 --> 00:20:38,550
Hey…

325
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:41,178
Shall I book an inn nearby?

326
00:20:41,261 --> 00:20:42,596
I'll stay there today.

327
00:20:42,679 --> 00:20:44,723
No, I can't make you do that.

328
00:20:44,806 --> 00:20:47,851
Then, how about we take turns?

329
00:20:48,435 --> 00:20:49,436
What?

330
00:20:53,398 --> 00:20:55,817
He's not coming out at all.

331
00:20:56,443 --> 00:20:57,903
He's so staying overnight.

332
00:20:57,986 --> 00:20:59,321
Be quiet for a bit!

333
00:20:59,404 --> 00:21:00,614
Sure.

334
00:21:29,184 --> 00:21:30,727
Here you go.

335
00:21:33,146 --> 00:21:34,439
Um…

336
00:21:34,981 --> 00:21:38,402
I've decided to close this place
at the end of this month.

337
00:21:38,485 --> 00:21:39,569
What?

338
00:21:40,278 --> 00:21:41,822
Why?

339
00:21:41,905 --> 00:21:45,117
I'm getting old, you know.

340
00:21:46,076 --> 00:21:47,369
Hey.

341
00:21:48,745 --> 00:21:49,996
What happened?

342
00:21:57,379 --> 00:22:01,675
It's embarrassing to admit,
but I fell for a scam.

343
00:22:02,175 --> 00:22:03,468
What?

344
00:22:04,010 --> 00:22:09,391
They told me I could get financial aid,
so I signed the papers without checking.

345
00:22:09,474 --> 00:22:11,017
But they were loan sharks.

346
00:22:12,853 --> 00:22:14,896
I'm such a fool, really.

347
00:22:15,564 --> 00:22:17,649
You're not a fool.

348
00:22:18,150 --> 00:22:20,569
The ones who tricked you
are the real fools.

349
00:22:26,408 --> 00:22:29,578
You didn't like the property
I showed you the other day?

350
00:22:29,661 --> 00:22:30,745
Yes.

351
00:22:30,829 --> 00:22:34,791
I'd prefer a place with as much
sunlight as possible.

352
00:22:34,875 --> 00:22:36,084
Sunlight?

353
00:22:37,335 --> 00:22:39,379
Sunlight, huh?

354
00:22:40,922 --> 00:22:42,591
May I use the restroom?

355
00:22:43,216 --> 00:22:45,010
Sure. Go ahead.

356
00:22:47,762 --> 00:22:49,723
It's down that hallway on the right.

357
00:22:49,806 --> 00:22:51,016
Thank you.

358
00:22:55,353 --> 00:22:56,396
Do you see it?

359
00:22:56,479 --> 00:22:57,731
I got it.

360
00:22:57,814 --> 00:22:59,399
Mr. Mukai!

361
00:23:01,651 --> 00:23:03,945
I told you not to come through the front.

362
00:23:05,614 --> 00:23:06,907
It went well, didn't it?

363
00:23:06,990 --> 00:23:09,284
That cafe owner was scared shitless.

364
00:23:09,367 --> 00:23:10,702
Seriously…

365
00:23:19,794 --> 00:23:20,629
Hey.

366
00:23:21,546 --> 00:23:23,506
Next time, come in from the back.

367
00:23:24,758 --> 00:23:25,842
Okay.

368
00:23:27,093 --> 00:23:27,969
Yes, sir.

369
00:23:32,182 --> 00:23:35,185
It seems he's colluding
with local racketeers

370
00:23:35,268 --> 00:23:37,562
to buy up land aggressively.

371
00:23:37,646 --> 00:23:40,774
So the true face of Mukai Real Estate

372
00:23:41,483 --> 00:23:42,943
is a bunch of land sharks.

373
00:23:43,026 --> 00:23:45,153
A terrible bunch.

374
00:23:47,113 --> 00:23:48,823
How far is it from the Expo?

375
00:23:48,907 --> 00:23:51,159
15 minutes by car, I suppose.

376
00:23:52,369 --> 00:23:53,203
This is

377
00:23:54,537 --> 00:23:56,915
the hidden blueprint.

378
00:24:04,547 --> 00:24:07,676
There's only one week
until the redevelopment announcement.

379
00:24:07,759 --> 00:24:11,096
Regional Development
is proceeding as planned.

380
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:14,641
How much will they buy it for?

381
00:24:14,724 --> 00:24:17,727
No doubt a huge sum of money.

382
00:24:17,811 --> 00:24:21,606
Once the money comes in,
I'll open a high-end club in Konan Ginza,

383
00:24:21,690 --> 00:24:24,442
and squeeze money out of the rich.

384
00:24:24,526 --> 00:24:26,152
You're terrible.

385
00:24:26,236 --> 00:24:31,366
More importantly, the problem is that
the old man Hoshino still hasn't given up.

386
00:24:31,449 --> 00:24:33,493
What a stubborn old man.

387
00:24:33,994 --> 00:24:35,495
I don't want to,

388
00:24:36,329 --> 00:24:39,165
but we might have
to make him suffer a bit.

389
00:24:39,249 --> 00:24:42,794
I don't want to get dragged into
such tedious matters.

390
00:24:43,295 --> 00:24:48,633
Once that lawyer is gone,
you can just harass him again.

391
00:24:49,634 --> 00:24:51,469
Leave the rest to me.

392
00:24:53,221 --> 00:24:55,181
I'll handle it.

393
00:25:19,789 --> 00:25:21,624
Do you have a moment?

394
00:25:25,754 --> 00:25:28,256
Things aren't going well, are they?

395
00:25:29,799 --> 00:25:31,176
I'm sorry.

396
00:25:32,218 --> 00:25:36,014
You must be wondering why I'm so attached
to a piece of land like this.

397
00:25:37,223 --> 00:25:39,434
My son tells me the same thing.

398
00:25:40,143 --> 00:25:43,188
He says it is safer to move
to a town close to a hospital.

399
00:25:43,813 --> 00:25:45,648
He's right about that.

400
00:25:46,816 --> 00:25:49,235
It would be more convenient too.

401
00:25:49,861 --> 00:25:51,863
Then, why?

402
00:26:01,247 --> 00:26:04,376
"I want to watch fireworks
with you again."

403
00:26:05,210 --> 00:26:06,044
What?

404
00:26:08,671 --> 00:26:10,590
My wife's last words.

405
00:26:16,721 --> 00:26:20,517
She went and died before me. That idiot!

406
00:26:25,563 --> 00:26:31,528
She liked watching
the fireworks from here.

407
00:26:36,825 --> 00:26:39,911
I don't have the slightest interest
in fireworks myself.

408
00:26:39,994 --> 00:26:42,580
They're noisy, and I don't
even think they're pretty.

409
00:26:42,664 --> 00:26:46,334
I don't care
for that merry atmosphere either.

410
00:26:47,127 --> 00:26:48,711
But still,

411
00:26:49,921 --> 00:26:54,342
I don't want to leave this land.

412
00:26:55,969 --> 00:27:00,557
I'm going to rebuild this place,
this rooftop too.

413
00:27:01,057 --> 00:27:03,309
I'll turn it into a home

414
00:27:03,393 --> 00:27:07,188
where my thick-headed son
and his family can return to and relax.

415
00:27:08,231 --> 00:27:11,776
I'll call them idiots and noisy.

416
00:27:12,652 --> 00:27:15,655
I'll drink alcohol
with my grandchild on my lap!

417
00:27:24,706 --> 00:27:27,709
It's enough. You can go home now.

418
00:27:28,710 --> 00:27:30,628
No, I must find evidence.

419
00:27:30,712 --> 00:27:31,588
You are

420
00:27:32,464 --> 00:27:35,216
an honest and earnest person.

421
00:27:36,718 --> 00:27:41,014
If there are still lawyers
like you around,

422
00:27:41,097 --> 00:27:43,475
the world may not be
entirely bad after all.

423
00:27:48,396 --> 00:27:49,606
This matter,

424
00:27:51,357 --> 00:27:54,360
I'll leave it all to you. Okay?

425
00:28:20,845 --> 00:28:25,225
The owner was friendly.
She even gave me some makgeolli.

426
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:41,366
Sorry for calling out of nowhere,
but that makgeolli you told me about…

427
00:28:41,449 --> 00:28:43,952
Oh, I forgot to take it home with me.

428
00:28:44,577 --> 00:28:48,331
Is it perhaps handmade there?

429
00:28:48,414 --> 00:28:49,791
Yeah, seems so.

430
00:28:49,874 --> 00:28:54,170
I drank it there and said it reminded me
of home, so she gave me some.

431
00:28:54,796 --> 00:28:56,714
Why? Is something wrong?

432
00:28:57,715 --> 00:29:01,636
In Japan, making alcohol
without a license is a crime.

433
00:29:01,719 --> 00:29:04,848
On top of that,
if she was serving it at the shop…

434
00:29:06,182 --> 00:29:08,226
-Shall we get started?
-Yes.

435
00:29:18,236 --> 00:29:19,362
-Hello.
-What's wrong?

436
00:29:19,445 --> 00:29:21,698
-I found a violation at the snack bar.
-What?

437
00:29:21,781 --> 00:29:23,867
We might be able
to solve this all at once.

438
00:30:00,737 --> 00:30:03,823
Uncovering lies with a false facade.

439
00:30:18,171 --> 00:30:19,714
Something bad has happened!

440
00:30:19,797 --> 00:30:23,301
Just now, someone from here
was hospitalized.

441
00:30:23,384 --> 00:30:24,385
What?

442
00:30:27,972 --> 00:30:30,141
KONAN GENERAL HOSPITAL

443
00:30:39,442 --> 00:30:44,489
I believe a Hiroshi Hoshino
was brought in here last night.

444
00:30:44,572 --> 00:30:46,491
I'll check.

445
00:30:47,742 --> 00:30:49,369
Mr. Hoshino is over there.

446
00:30:50,662 --> 00:30:51,746
Follow me.

447
00:31:00,421 --> 00:31:02,090
He's heading there now.

448
00:31:02,757 --> 00:31:04,634
HIROSHI HOSHINO

449
00:31:05,468 --> 00:31:06,678
Here it is.

450
00:31:09,806 --> 00:31:11,140
Excuse me.

451
00:31:14,978 --> 00:31:16,270
How can I help you?

452
00:31:16,354 --> 00:31:18,940
May I see Mr. Hoshino?

453
00:31:19,023 --> 00:31:21,067
He is still resting right now.

454
00:31:21,567 --> 00:31:23,361
I see.

455
00:31:23,444 --> 00:31:25,530
Doctor, thank you very much.

456
00:31:25,613 --> 00:31:26,739
It's nothing.

457
00:31:27,991 --> 00:31:33,079
Huh? Excuse me, are you Mr. Hoshino's…

458
00:31:34,163 --> 00:31:35,581
Are you my father's friend?

459
00:31:35,665 --> 00:31:38,376
Father? Oh, um, I…

460
00:31:38,459 --> 00:31:42,338
I manage Mr. Hoshino's apartment building.

461
00:31:42,422 --> 00:31:44,382
My name is Mukai.

462
00:31:45,216 --> 00:31:46,634
Are you his son?

463
00:31:46,718 --> 00:31:47,885
Yes.

464
00:31:47,969 --> 00:31:50,304
I am his son. You can call me Taichi.

465
00:31:51,556 --> 00:31:52,890
-Mr. Mukai.
-Yes.

466
00:31:53,474 --> 00:31:56,019
I must discuss something
with you downstairs.

467
00:31:56,519 --> 00:31:57,687
Excuse me.

468
00:32:00,023 --> 00:32:01,482
Thank you very much.

469
00:32:01,566 --> 00:32:03,818
-Will he be okay?
-I don't know.

470
00:32:23,087 --> 00:32:24,255
Excuse me.

471
00:32:24,964 --> 00:32:26,799
I'm here to talk about your alcohol--

472
00:32:26,883 --> 00:32:28,593
It's not my fault, you know!

473
00:32:28,676 --> 00:32:29,510
What?

474
00:32:29,594 --> 00:32:33,431
Old man Hoshino collapsed.
I have nothing to do with it!

475
00:32:33,514 --> 00:32:34,766
He collapsed?

476
00:32:43,524 --> 00:32:45,902
My father is already 75 years old,

477
00:32:46,486 --> 00:32:49,447
and as you can see, his health isn't good.

478
00:32:49,530 --> 00:32:51,491
So,

479
00:32:52,575 --> 00:32:55,119
I would like to sell
that apartment building.

480
00:32:55,203 --> 00:32:56,287
What?

481
00:32:56,871 --> 00:33:00,374
I worry about my father staying there…

482
00:33:02,085 --> 00:33:03,711
Sorry for the short notice.

483
00:33:04,378 --> 00:33:06,839
I have to return to Seoul tomorrow.

484
00:33:10,301 --> 00:33:11,719
I see.

485
00:33:14,180 --> 00:33:17,558
When he collapsed before,
my father gave me power of attorney.

486
00:33:17,642 --> 00:33:20,812
He said, "If anything happens,
I'm leaving things to you."

487
00:33:21,813 --> 00:33:24,440
I understand your situation.

488
00:33:24,524 --> 00:33:25,650
Excuse me.

489
00:33:25,733 --> 00:33:27,985
Mr. Hoshino, do you have a moment?

490
00:33:28,069 --> 00:33:29,529
Yes.

491
00:33:38,079 --> 00:33:42,166
We have a problem. I got a call from Habu.
It seems Ms. Aso is heading here.

492
00:33:42,250 --> 00:33:43,626
-Hurry.
-Hey!

493
00:33:46,587 --> 00:33:47,755
A script?

494
00:33:49,173 --> 00:33:51,509
-Ms. Aso has arrived.
-Oh no! Just go!

495
00:33:51,592 --> 00:33:54,345
Hey! Well, okay.

496
00:33:58,516 --> 00:33:59,392
There she is.

497
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:03,271
The script!

498
00:34:03,771 --> 00:34:06,482
Nakazaki! Nakazaki, the script!

499
00:34:13,447 --> 00:34:16,200
Donghyuk? I'm at the hospital.

500
00:34:17,994 --> 00:34:18,995
What?

501
00:34:19,078 --> 00:34:22,039
I am Kimura, a judicial scrivener.

502
00:34:22,123 --> 00:34:23,708
Please take a seat.

503
00:34:23,791 --> 00:34:26,669
Without further ado,

504
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:32,758
please allow me to verify the identity
of Mr. Taichi Hoshino.

505
00:34:32,842 --> 00:34:33,926
Go ahead, sir.

506
00:34:34,010 --> 00:34:36,512
Could you please state

507
00:34:36,596 --> 00:34:41,517
your father's and your own date of birth?

508
00:34:41,601 --> 00:34:45,188
My father was born on August 20th, 1951.

509
00:34:45,271 --> 00:34:49,025
I was born on December 5th, 1991.

510
00:34:49,108 --> 00:34:53,112
Next, where is the nearest
convenience store from here?

511
00:34:53,196 --> 00:34:55,865
AB Mart, a 20-minute walk.

512
00:35:00,161 --> 00:35:03,247
Now, next…

513
00:35:03,873 --> 00:35:05,291
Here…

514
00:35:07,210 --> 00:35:12,048
The vacated lot to the left of your house
used to be a store. Which one?

515
00:35:14,842 --> 00:35:17,803
The photos are upside down.

516
00:35:21,432 --> 00:35:22,350
Mr. Taichi?

517
00:35:30,650 --> 00:35:37,156
Which shop did the vacant lot use to be?

518
00:35:39,492 --> 00:35:40,785
Sabayama!

519
00:35:41,452 --> 00:35:44,330
Excuse me, may I use the restroom?

520
00:35:47,124 --> 00:35:48,251
Huh?

521
00:35:49,460 --> 00:35:52,713
It's not here!

522
00:35:54,048 --> 00:35:55,258
He went to the toilet?

523
00:36:00,012 --> 00:36:01,097
Hello?

524
00:36:01,180 --> 00:36:02,932
Hello?

525
00:36:03,015 --> 00:36:04,767
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

526
00:36:04,850 --> 00:36:06,227
What's wrong?

527
00:36:06,310 --> 00:36:10,648
I don't know if it's the butcher shop
or the sweets shop.

528
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:13,651
He probably means
the vacant lot next door.

529
00:36:13,734 --> 00:36:16,279
-What did you say?
-Relax. I'll tell you right now.

530
00:36:16,362 --> 00:36:18,447
-Hurry!
-The sweets shop!

531
00:36:18,531 --> 00:36:20,700
-The sweets shop.
-It's the sweets shop.

532
00:36:20,783 --> 00:36:23,077
Hello? Why hang up so suddenly?

533
00:36:23,911 --> 00:36:27,498
What? Why now?

534
00:36:27,581 --> 00:36:29,583
Mr. Taichi, are you okay?

535
00:36:29,667 --> 00:36:30,835
Yes.

536
00:36:32,211 --> 00:36:33,963
I'm okay!

537
00:36:37,341 --> 00:36:39,510
HOT SPRINGS INN WAKABA

538
00:36:44,307 --> 00:36:45,266
Ms. Aso.

539
00:36:45,349 --> 00:36:47,601
I heard that Mr. Hoshino was hospitalized.

540
00:36:49,854 --> 00:36:51,022
Dad!

541
00:36:51,105 --> 00:36:53,149
Why did you come back, Taichi?

542
00:36:53,232 --> 00:36:57,069
I heard things were going nowhere
with the snack bar, so I rushed back.

543
00:36:57,570 --> 00:36:58,654
Why are you here?

544
00:36:58,738 --> 00:37:02,450
Yesterday, someone from the inn
came to pick me up,

545
00:37:02,533 --> 00:37:04,493
saying you asked them to.

546
00:37:05,244 --> 00:37:08,122
This was your surprise gift, right?

547
00:37:13,419 --> 00:37:15,212
The real Taichi has returned.

548
00:37:15,296 --> 00:37:16,547
Sabayama is done for.

549
00:37:16,630 --> 00:37:17,798
Pardon?

550
00:37:17,882 --> 00:37:21,469
We talked to Mukai at the hospital.
Only you can save him, Habu.

551
00:37:21,552 --> 00:37:22,636
Please!

552
00:37:24,013 --> 00:37:25,681
Got it.

553
00:37:30,811 --> 00:37:33,773
You must have many memories of the place.

554
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:53,793
I've answered enough already!

555
00:37:54,377 --> 00:37:55,336
What?

556
00:37:59,590 --> 00:38:03,010
Mr. Mukai, how is it going?
Did you find a property for me?

557
00:38:03,094 --> 00:38:06,389
No, Mr. Habuta, I'm a bit busy right now.

558
00:38:06,472 --> 00:38:09,392
I'm sorry to interrupt.

559
00:38:09,475 --> 00:38:11,352
-Then…
-I'll find one for you.

560
00:38:11,435 --> 00:38:13,020
I'm counting on you.

561
00:38:14,271 --> 00:38:15,398
Sorry.

562
00:38:16,148 --> 00:38:17,441
Excuse me.

563
00:38:20,861 --> 00:38:21,904
Sorry for that.

564
00:38:27,034 --> 00:38:29,161
It's not this one.

565
00:38:29,912 --> 00:38:32,081
It's this sweets shop.

566
00:38:41,966 --> 00:38:43,926
USED TO BE A SWEETS SHOP

567
00:38:56,147 --> 00:38:58,149
HIROSHI HOSHINO

568
00:39:00,985 --> 00:39:02,194
I've received it.

569
00:39:03,237 --> 00:39:05,114
I'll transfer the money later.

570
00:39:05,197 --> 00:39:07,658
Give my regards to your father.

571
00:39:07,741 --> 00:39:09,326
Thank you very much.

572
00:39:22,506 --> 00:39:26,927
Hey, old man Hoshino finally gave in.

573
00:39:27,011 --> 00:39:31,515
I'll throw in extra money as promised
and transfer it to you. Sign this for me.

574
00:39:32,224 --> 00:39:33,893
What did you do to him?

575
00:39:33,976 --> 00:39:35,811
Nothing.

576
00:39:37,188 --> 00:39:38,898
Come on, hurry up.

577
00:39:38,981 --> 00:39:40,065
Okay?

578
00:39:42,109 --> 00:39:43,152
All right.

579
00:39:46,447 --> 00:39:47,573
Mr. Habuta?

580
00:39:49,158 --> 00:39:52,745
You ended up moving out after all.

581
00:39:53,245 --> 00:39:54,246
What?

582
00:39:55,789 --> 00:39:58,417
Sounds like it, Mr. Hoshino.

583
00:40:00,753 --> 00:40:01,795
Mr. Hoshino?

584
00:40:02,379 --> 00:40:04,632
-Aren't you in the hospital?
-Hospital?

585
00:40:04,715 --> 00:40:08,177
Just a moment ago,
your son came to my shop and…

586
00:40:08,260 --> 00:40:10,513
Huh? Hey!

587
00:40:10,596 --> 00:40:12,389
Did you go there?

588
00:40:12,473 --> 00:40:14,141
No, I didn't.

589
00:40:15,392 --> 00:40:16,685
Who are you?

590
00:40:16,769 --> 00:40:18,062
I'm his son, Taichi.

591
00:40:18,979 --> 00:40:19,980
Wait.

592
00:40:20,064 --> 00:40:21,690
What does this mean?

593
00:40:23,400 --> 00:40:27,238
I am his son. You can call me Taichi.
I was born on December 5th, 1991.

594
00:40:29,031 --> 00:40:30,533
Was I tricked?

595
00:40:31,033 --> 00:40:33,369
Oh no! My money!

596
00:40:36,956 --> 00:40:39,083
Hey, wait a minute!

597
00:40:44,505 --> 00:40:47,383
Mr. Hoshino, this is the eviction notice.

598
00:40:47,466 --> 00:40:48,592
Really?

599
00:40:49,927 --> 00:40:51,387
Mr. Mukai!

600
00:40:51,470 --> 00:40:52,388
Dad!

601
00:41:01,939 --> 00:41:05,276
And so, of course,
the sales contract is invalid.

602
00:41:05,359 --> 00:41:08,612
We were also able to kick out
the snack bar owner. It all ended well.

603
00:41:08,696 --> 00:41:11,073
It's not "well" at all.

604
00:41:11,156 --> 00:41:14,326
Renting that inn was the highest expense.

605
00:41:14,410 --> 00:41:16,870
Your acting was great too, Sabayama.

606
00:41:16,954 --> 00:41:20,457
Just so you know, I'm an architect.

607
00:41:20,541 --> 00:41:22,334
"I've answered enough already!"

608
00:41:22,418 --> 00:41:23,586
I didn't say it like that.

609
00:41:23,669 --> 00:41:26,046
Mr. Uramawashi made the bar owner confess,

610
00:41:26,130 --> 00:41:29,383
and Mukai's misdeeds
came to light one after another.

611
00:41:30,593 --> 00:41:34,847
That coffee shop also got compensation.
They'll reopen in front of the station.

612
00:41:37,057 --> 00:41:38,058
LAND SHARKS IN KONAN CITY

613
00:41:38,142 --> 00:41:41,020
Did you target
Mukai Real Estate from the start?

614
00:41:41,103 --> 00:41:42,062
Who knows.

615
00:41:42,146 --> 00:41:43,981
Please don't play innocent.

616
00:41:44,064 --> 00:41:47,610
You realized that Konan City
was connected to that Expo project,

617
00:41:47,693 --> 00:41:51,071
so you let me run free
while waiting for Mukai to show his tail.

618
00:41:51,155 --> 00:41:52,364
Am I right?

619
00:41:52,448 --> 00:41:54,283
If that's the case, then what?

620
00:41:54,366 --> 00:41:59,079
If that's the case, that means
I was your unwitting pawn, wasn't I?

621
00:41:59,163 --> 00:42:00,331
Correct.

622
00:42:00,414 --> 00:42:01,498
What?

623
00:42:06,003 --> 00:42:07,838
In Le Corbusier's Plan Voisin,

624
00:42:07,921 --> 00:42:10,132
he took advantage
of the traffic congestion

625
00:42:10,215 --> 00:42:12,259
and environmental problems in Paris

626
00:42:12,343 --> 00:42:14,928
to propose a new
three-dimensional urban plan

627
00:42:15,012 --> 00:42:17,389
that actively promoted transportation.

628
00:42:17,473 --> 00:42:19,016
Here you go again.

629
00:42:27,316 --> 00:42:31,028
I commend you for earning the trust
of that stubborn old man Hoshino.

630
00:42:31,111 --> 00:42:33,530
However, even assuming

631
00:42:34,698 --> 00:42:37,785
you kicked out the snack bar owner,

632
00:42:37,868 --> 00:42:41,080
Mukai was the true land shark
behind the scenes, wasn't he?

633
00:42:42,831 --> 00:42:44,667
If things had continued like that,

634
00:42:44,750 --> 00:42:48,837
they would have used every trick
in the book to corner Mr. Hoshino

635
00:42:48,921 --> 00:42:51,131
until they got their hands on that land.

636
00:42:51,215 --> 00:42:52,466
If that had happened,

637
00:42:53,759 --> 00:42:57,012
even his life could have been in danger.

638
00:42:57,096 --> 00:42:58,931
Didn't you think of that?

639
00:43:00,057 --> 00:43:01,183
But…

640
00:43:01,266 --> 00:43:04,269
Against an opponent
who doesn't listen to common sense…

641
00:43:05,229 --> 00:43:08,023
Justice alone won't work.

642
00:43:10,025 --> 00:43:11,151
Even so, I--

643
00:43:11,860 --> 00:43:14,154
Fight poison with poison.

644
00:43:15,572 --> 00:43:17,866
There are times when that is necessary.

645
00:43:21,370 --> 00:43:25,416
So, Uramawashi was involved after all?

646
00:43:26,083 --> 00:43:27,668
I'm sorry.

647
00:43:27,751 --> 00:43:30,295
By the time I realized,
the damage was done.

648
00:43:31,463 --> 00:43:32,548
Well,

649
00:43:33,549 --> 00:43:37,428
I won't ask what he did.

650
00:43:41,014 --> 00:43:43,517
Is my way of doing things wrong?

651
00:43:46,437 --> 00:43:48,230
Sorry for this strange question.

652
00:43:48,981 --> 00:43:50,065
Not at all.

653
00:43:51,400 --> 00:43:55,195
I don't think you are wrong.

654
00:43:58,031 --> 00:44:00,534
However, eventually,

655
00:44:01,618 --> 00:44:03,787
between law and justice,

656
00:44:03,871 --> 00:44:06,915
a time will come
when your convictions are tested.

657
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:10,502
That's what I believe, Ms. Aso.

658
00:44:18,302 --> 00:44:22,514
Mr. Hoshino,
won't you allow us to purchase the land?

659
00:44:23,182 --> 00:44:24,099
What?

660
00:44:24,183 --> 00:44:29,688
To give you peace of mind, we'll buy it
at a price higher than market rate.

661
00:44:32,024 --> 00:44:33,525
Look at this property.

662
00:44:34,276 --> 00:44:36,069
Donghyuk introduced it to me.

663
00:44:36,945 --> 00:44:39,656
It's close to the hospital
and very accessible.

664
00:44:42,743 --> 00:44:43,827
Dad.

665
00:44:43,911 --> 00:44:46,079
Consider this my request too.

666
00:44:48,665 --> 00:44:53,045
From the balcony of that new home,
you can clearly see the fireworks.

667
00:44:57,090 --> 00:45:00,594
He will pass through here.
Please keep it clear.

668
00:45:00,677 --> 00:45:02,304
Thank you very much.

669
00:45:13,148 --> 00:45:15,108
You're all talk!

670
00:45:15,192 --> 00:45:17,611
-Don't get cocky!
-Give me back my taxes!

671
00:45:19,321 --> 00:45:21,031
Please trust me.

672
00:45:21,907 --> 00:45:22,991
What?

673
00:45:25,953 --> 00:45:28,330
I will change Konan City…

674
00:45:28,413 --> 00:45:31,875
No, I will definitely change Japan.

675
00:45:37,381 --> 00:45:39,424
JUSTICE'S FORM
PLEASE GIVE IT A READ

676
00:45:46,974 --> 00:45:48,767
A house haunted by demons?

677
00:45:49,268 --> 00:45:50,561
You must be scared.

678
00:45:50,644 --> 00:45:52,104
I'm not scared!

679
00:45:52,187 --> 00:45:55,232
It's cute how terrible you are at lying.

680
00:45:55,315 --> 00:45:58,026
If you make light of it,
you'll end up regretting it.

681
00:45:58,110 --> 00:46:00,237
They should be here soon.

682
00:46:01,321 --> 00:46:03,657
I've been a troublesome kid
since I was little.

683
00:46:04,825 --> 00:46:06,243
You won't contradict me?

684
00:46:07,536 --> 00:46:08,495
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

